WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.684
<v Examiner>The ovarian and uterine cycles.

2
00:00:03.684 --> 00:00:04.418
<v Examiner>Six marks.

3
00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:09.205
<v Examiner>Describe the phases of the ovarian and uterine cycles in the female,

4
00:00:09.205 --> 00:00:11.183
<v Examiner>and how the hormones link them.

5
00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:13.978
She posted no model answer for this one,

6
00:00:13.978 --> 00:00:17.497
so this answer is built straight from her Repro Female deck.

7
00:00:17.497 --> 00:00:21.601
It's six marks, and it comes back in the final, in the fertility case,

8
00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:23.067
so it's worth the effort.

9
00:00:23.517 --> 00:00:27.473
Two cycles run side by side: the ovary's, and the uterus's.

10
00:00:27.473 --> 00:00:30.088
Day one is the first day of the period.

11
00:00:30.538 --> 00:00:31.158
The hook.

12
00:00:31.158 --> 00:00:34.326
The ovary: grow, pop, yellow body, white scar.

13
00:00:34.326 --> 00:00:36.874
The uterus: shed, rebuild, get ready.

14
00:00:37.324 --> 00:00:38.479
The ovary first.

15
00:00:38.479 --> 00:00:41.583
The follicular phase, days one to fourteen.

16
00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:47.790
FSH from the anterior pituitary makes a follicle grow: primordial, primary, secondary,

17
00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.389
and then a mature Graafian follicle.

18
00:00:50.389 --> 00:00:53.132
Its granulosa cells secrete oestrogen.

19
00:00:53.582 --> 00:00:56.729
Ovulation, mid-cycle, at about day fourteen.

20
00:00:56.729 --> 00:01:02.664
A surge of LH makes the Graafian follicle rupture and release the secondary oocyte.

21
00:01:02.664 --> 00:01:03.737
That's the pop.

22
00:01:04.187 --> 00:01:07.227
The luteal phase, days fourteen to twenty-eight.

23
00:01:07.227 --> 00:01:11.345
The ruptured follicle becomes the corpus luteum, the yellow body,

24
00:01:11.345 --> 00:01:14.386
which secretes progesterone, and some oestrogen.

25
00:01:14.386 --> 00:01:19.834
If there's no pregnancy, it breaks down after about ten days into the corpus albicans,

26
00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:20.784
the white scar.

27
00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:23.270
Now the uterus.

28
00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:25.896
The menstrual phase, days one to five.

29
00:01:25.896 --> 00:01:29.074
Progesterone falls, the spiral arteries spasm,

30
00:01:29.074 --> 00:01:32.943
and the stratum functionalis of the endometrium is shed.

31
00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:36.441
The proliferative phase, days six to fourteen.

32
00:01:36.441 --> 00:01:40.945
Rising oestrogen from the growing follicle rebuilds the endometrium.

33
00:01:41.395 --> 00:01:44.688
The secretory phase, days fifteen to twenty-eight.

34
00:01:44.688 --> 00:01:50.153
Progesterone from the corpus luteum turns the endometrium into a gland-rich lining,

35
00:01:50.153 --> 00:01:51.668
ready for implantation.

36
00:01:51.668 --> 00:01:56.475
If no embryo implants, the corpus luteum breaks down, progesterone falls,

37
00:01:56.475 --> 00:01:58.450
and menstruation starts again.

38
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:02.665
That fall in progesterone is the link that restarts both cycles.

39
00:02:04.115 --> 00:02:04.821
The traps.

40
00:02:04.821 --> 00:02:08.283
The follicular phase goes with FSH and oestrogen.

41
00:02:08.283 --> 00:02:12.664
The luteal phase goes with the corpus luteum and progesterone.

42
00:02:12.664 --> 00:02:17.328
Second: proliferative is oestrogen, and secretory is progesterone.

43
00:02:17.328 --> 00:02:20.507
Third: only the stratum functionalis is shed.

44
00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:24.040
The stratum basalis stays, and grows the next one.

45
00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:25.188
<v Examiner>Once more.

46
00:02:25.188 --> 00:02:26.026
<v Examiner>Both cycles.

47
00:02:28.476 --> 00:02:29.696
The ovarian cycle.

48
00:02:29.696 --> 00:02:34.845
In the follicular phase, FSH makes a follicle grow into a Graafian follicle,

49
00:02:34.845 --> 00:02:36.538
which secretes oestrogen.

50
00:02:36.538 --> 00:02:38.842
At ovulation, around day fourteen,

51
00:02:38.842 --> 00:02:42.771
an LH surge ruptures it and releases the secondary oocyte.

52
00:02:42.771 --> 00:02:46.836
In the luteal phase the corpus luteum secretes progesterone,

53
00:02:46.836 --> 00:02:50.563
and without a pregnancy it becomes the corpus albicans.

54
00:02:50.563 --> 00:02:51.782
The uterine cycle.

55
00:02:51.782 --> 00:02:57.202
In the menstrual phase, progesterone falls and the stratum functionalis is shed.

56
00:02:57.202 --> 00:03:00.590
In the proliferative phase, oestrogen rebuilds it.

57
00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:04.993
In the secretory phase, progesterone readies it for implantation.

58
00:03:04.993 --> 00:03:09.871
With no implantation, progesterone falls, and menstruation starts again.
